G53.1 on a table-table machine, xyzac-trt-kins: both rotaries carry the
work, so the pose is named by the sign of the one that carries the other,
A here, as Heidenhain's SEQ names its master axis.  For each plane, from
several starting poses: G53.1 with no P takes the nearer of the two poses,
P1 always the one with A positive and P2 the one with A negative, the same
pose from every start; each leaves the tool along the plane's normal; a
move in the plane after the turn ends where the plane puts it.

Then again with A tilting one way only, [AXIS_A] 0 to 100 while [JOINT_3]
runs on to 9999: G53.1 to each side plane goes to A90 with C carrying the
side round, never to A270, a whole turn the joint has travel for and the
axis has not.
